# TASK/SYSINFO02, EmuDESK (no #Z), C:\CMDLINE.TXT seeded with cmdline-seed.txt:
# open the System Info dialog from the Desk menu (as desk.actions), then
#   Memory protection drop-down (486,229) -> hover "Strict" (486,245) -> click
#   Block cache drop-down (486,317) -> hover "8 MB" (486,285) -> click
#   Serial console drop-down (486,383) -> hover "Off" (486,399) -> click
#   outside the box (200,383, the "Running now" column) = cancel
#   Save (73,455) -> the confirmation alert -> Return (its default "Save")
#   Return (the dialog's DEFAULT OK; nothing unsaved) closes the dialog.
# Coordinates from the calibration dump cal-open-D02_DIALOG.png (dialog root
# at (14,23); drop-down rows 22 px apart from y 221; a drop-down puts the
# current choice over its button, items 16 px high).
# Every mark lies >= 200 ticks before the next input: drive-m3.py takes the
# dump --mark-delay host seconds AFTER the mark line (0.5 s = 100 ticks at
# 200 Hz), so a mark closer to the next input may show the state after it
# (the try1/try2 runs did -- see RUNINFO). Esc is not used: it does not reach
# the accessory (diag.actions, RUNINFO "Esc").
# Ticks hz_200 after "[desk] desktop up" (desk-arm-m3.py). IKBD Return 1C/9C.
100 parkbr
400 mark E00_IDLE
500 move 26 9
800 mark E00_DESK_OPEN
1000 move 60 66
1200 down
1203 up
2000 mark E01_DIALOG
2300 move 486 229
2400 down
2403 up
2700 move 486 245
2800 mark E02_POPUP_MEMPROT
3000 down
3003 up
3200 mark E03_MEMPROT_STRICT
3400 move 486 317
3500 down
3503 up
3800 move 486 285
3900 mark E04_POPUP_BCACHE
4100 down
4103 up
4300 mark E05_TWO_CHANGED
4500 move 486 383
4600 down
4603 up
4900 move 486 399
5000 mark E06_POPUP_SERIAL
5200 move 200 383
5300 down
5303 up
5450 mark E07_OUTSIDE_CANCELLED
5600 move 73 455
5700 down
5703 up
5900 mark E08_CONFIRM
6200 key 1C
6206 key 9C
6500 mark E09_SAVED
6800 key 1C
6806 key 9C
7200 mark E10_CLOSED
7300 parkbr
7600 mark END
